<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Niugini Mining reports year net loss.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Niugini Mining reports year net loss.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>		   (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net			     loss   38.91 vs profit 5.02</p>
<p>    Operating		     loss   14.60 vs profit 5.02</p>
<p>    Abnormal			loss   24.32 vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Niugini Mining is a gold miner with interests in Papua New Guinea. It is 50.4 percent-owned by Battle Mountain Gold Co.  </p>
<p>    Sales				   79.19 vs 91.56</p>
<p>    Tax					 nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)		     loss 33.1 vs 5.3</p>
<p>    Interest				  nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  19.83 vs 24.67</p>
<p>Note: Niugini has a 17.5 percent stake in PNG's Lihir gold mine. It said abnormal loss included US$15.728 million writedown on value of San Cristobal mine in Chile, a US$6.58 million write-off of the Mungana and Three Sisters operations, and US$2.01 million in executive severance pay.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
